  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "To prepare the ingredients, dice the onion and tomato. Cut the cauliflower into florets and chop the mint. Drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/555430e0fd2cb9ae048b456d/step_556eb31f179f1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the olive oil in a medium saucepan over a low-medium heat. Add the onion, stir then leave covered for about 8 minutes or until it is soft."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the HelloFresh curry mix, cauliflower and a good grind of black pepper. Stir to combine then add the tomatoes and chickpeas, use a spoon to break up the tomatoes a little. Cover and simmer on a medium heat for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally (if you want a thicker curry leave the lid off). The curry is ready when the cauliflower is tender, so after 10 minutes take a peek and keep checking until you are happy. Remove from heat and stir through half of the yoghurt. Season with a bit of salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/555430e0fd2cb9ae048b456d/step_556eb31f45442.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide between serving bowls, serve with remaining yoghurt and a sprinkle of mint leaves.\n• Did you know? The Romans believed the scent of mint would stop a person from losing his temper, some royal ambassadors carried mint sprigs in their pockets."
    }
